#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507535} :activity/id #uuid "61f74d27-8967-5278-99ab-939f2c9f5d63" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049553 :topic/id #uuid "fed8aeb7-cb56-5ca6-9352-ed88fd02f45e" :topic/math-academy-id 3636} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507535 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176262 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5559f4b-1521-523b-8406-0bc5d66dde15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173833} {:answer/id #uuid "0256d74d-a236-57b6-be17-032aa4d685c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173834} {:answer/id #uuid "5d4e18a3-88e7-5f78-901b-41cc43b03702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506903} {:answer/id #uuid "8b6fd457-4eb9-5f91-a02c-38afa9b1bc0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506988} {:answer/id #uuid "eb17bacf-1aea-52d5-8089-fcb79fd9e5c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507198}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506903} :answer-field/id #uuid "d58894b2-ff7d-514e-beee-5c2f7fe8ec3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d2b8ae16-dd41-57f5-a30f-634ebab68387" :question/math-academy-id "q-110422" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4xy, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe marginal CDF ${F}_{X}(x)$ of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ g(x), & 0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 1 & x>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the function $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4xy\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4x{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =2x[{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =2x({1}^{2}-0) \\\\  & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the marginal CDF of $X$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}{f}_{X}(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}2u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={[{u}^{2}]}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-0 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${F}_{X}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {x}^{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 1 & x>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $g(x)={x}^{2}.$"} :step/id #uuid "0ffd72bb-a8c0-5855-b23b-6732826ff26e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507544}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507544 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507488 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ea94da0-212f-53c3-a486-393d1299b039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-4{x}^{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506906} {:answer/id #uuid "7fdfe9ca-4b60-5702-9714-ab58418f727d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-6{x}^{5}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506960} {:answer/id #uuid "a54fc47c-9a0e-57b6-8b89-be9050bd877c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6{x}^{2}-5{x}^{4}}{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507037} {:answer/id #uuid "eea6aa59-5b2f-56da-964c-d354c3437006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{2}-12{x}^{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507204} {:answer/id #uuid "f64e3710-d943-541a-b12e-b9944246e6ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{15({x}^{2}-{x}^{4})}{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507221}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507221} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e637269-5e6b-5cf4-8954-d277add9508e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bc9a9ffe-ea0b-5f0e-a6de-e484fad54774" :question/math-academy-id "q-142703" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with a joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=15{x}^{2}y,\\,x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1.\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{X}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1\\}.$\n\n![](images/df/dfa15482cfa0e8fdc9e98b05a71d2b64a89b3886da44f6966fee9f1b5e096eef.png)\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}15{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =15{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =15{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}[{x}^{2}{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}[{x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}})}^{2}-{x}^{2}\\cdot {0}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}[{x}^{2}\\cdot (1-{x}^{2})-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{15({x}^{2}-{x}^{4})}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{15({x}^{2}-{x}^{4})}{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "31d77338-adef-522f-8da7-bc7e285aec17" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507554}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507554 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507428 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49ad0885-f8da-524f-9005-e5e1b037ad4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y-2{y}^{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506853} {:answer/id #uuid "7115d60d-e9d8-5f83-a19f-079b5ac98a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{2}, & 0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506938} {:answer/id #uuid "7e391690-8700-5883-ae9c-3a383d2225f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4}, & 0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506955} {:answer/id #uuid "a0cf1e33-8ff7-5254-a612-ffb05d938e3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6y-3{y}^{2}}{4}, & 0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507023} {:answer/id #uuid "e1bf8a30-3690-5c0d-8f4e-7c1805175b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4}, & 0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507171}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507171} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0102b4d-840b-5f84-bda9-896fcec58961" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "43cc234d-7098-5a99-82b7-39099388a118" :question/math-academy-id "q-142707" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with a joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{xy}{2},\\,x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4.\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{Y}(y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4\\}.$\n\n![](images/f6/f65ef4fc9d7ae895bc7ba8fe99bc7b03d8b26c92611fcbc43f600aa2e0c30301.png)\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $0\\le y\\le 2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\frac{xy}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}xy\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}y]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[{x}^{2}y]_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[{(\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}})}^{2}\\cdot y-{0}^{2}\\cdot y] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(4-{y}^{2})y-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[4y-{y}^{3}] \\\\  & =y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4}, & 0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "5ea203c3-b8b6-5671-9cd4-e1bd1eb943ad" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507565}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507565 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507417 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20316b3d-871f-52f5-b903-85bdc45f6d27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.3536" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506741} {:answer/id #uuid "677bc76f-78b2-58a6-be32-39f8b6cf5041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506921} {:answer/id #uuid "aa3dbd41-a77d-56c3-871d-26a1c27b3178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507053} {:answer/id #uuid "e7a695a9-e856-5582-be47-9f7aea992d16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.8348" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507189} {:answer/id #uuid "f8ba3ad6-e42c-5fa6-bd84-8efbfdfdfc34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.1768" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507225}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506741} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b0c6ed0-18fa-583a-b1bb-5250eadea4f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507323}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3631ecfc-d4a3-5620-abd5-3d7860073884" :question/math-academy-id "q-142908" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt{x}\\,y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,2\\le y\\le 3, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X<0.5).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt{x}\\,y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{10}\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}]}_{y=2}^{y=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\sqrt{x}({3}^{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{x}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<0.5) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0.5}{f}_{X}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{0.5}(\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3/2}]}_{0}^{0.5} \\\\  & =[{0.5}^{3/2}]-[{0}^{3/2}] \\\\  & ≈0.3536.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8e3d3759-ee1e-5e5e-ada8-644f3c813177" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507586}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507586 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507402 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "013c2556-2676-5788-87c5-ed7f14fbe60e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506680} {:answer/id #uuid "3376b66e-72f1-521c-9aa1-68703ead3d4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506803} {:answer/id #uuid "58549a00-2751-552c-af49-cc906a42a61d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506881} {:answer/id #uuid "63a2b90c-fbfd-585e-af5d-498e3093f055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506914} {:answer/id #uuid "e1b57d6d-be30-5d75-a19b-cec00a3bf106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507170}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506881} :answer-field/id #uuid "00986474-0f08-5b7b-8afa-1dc60c06bfa3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0b0ce4fe-46e8-561a-bdf9-b2690fdeeb0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-142909" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{19}x\\sqrt{y}, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,4\\le y\\le 9, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X\\ge 1.9).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $1\\le x\\le 2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{4}^{9}\\frac{1}{19}x\\sqrt{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{19}x{[\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3/2}]}_{y=4}^{y=9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{57}x{[{y}^{3/2}]}_{y=4}^{y=9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{57}x({9}^{3/2}-{4}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}x, & 1\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 1.9) & ={\\int }_{1.9}^{\\infty }{f}_{X}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1.9}^{2}\\frac{2}{3}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{1.9}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[{2}^{2}-{1.9}^{2}] \\\\  & =0.13.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e3721229-b361-5d7c-96cf-50883a304a69"}] :activity/title "Marginal Distributions for Continuous Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506669}]}
